    "text": "Consider a region of space in which constant, uniform, and mutually perpendicular fields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">→</mo></mover></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;exists. Now a particle of charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;enters this region with a velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;which is&nbsp;perpendicular to both the fields.&nbsp;If the velocity of the charge remains unchanged, then"
